# Shell scripts must be checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites these files
# to CRLF. bash then reads `set -euo pipefail` as `pipefail\r` and dies with
# "invalid option name" — so the overlay tests passed on WSL and failed on
# Windows from a clean checkout. Declaring the rule here fixes every checkout
# at once; making the test rewrite a temp copy would have hidden the same bug
# from anyone running the script directly.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The workflow is executed by GitHub on Linux; keep its line endings stable so
# a Windows editor cannot introduce invisible differences.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
